SUMMARY:Roy Wood Jr. LIVE at Blue Note Hawaii (Late Show)
DTSTAMP:20260824T033957Z
DTSTART:20260827T203000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate l
	inks. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Perfor
	mer\nRoy Wood Jr. is one of the most versatile and celebrated comedians wo
	rking today. An Emmy-nominated comedian\, documentary producer\, WGA-nomin
	ated writer\, actor\, and radio personality\, Wood Jr. is best known for h
	is eight years as a correspondent on Comedy Central’s Emmy-winning The Dai
	ly Show (2015–2023). \nIn 2023\, he guest hosted The Daily Show and headli
	ned the White House Correspondents’ Dinner to its highest ratings since 20
	17. His fourth stand-up special\, Lonely Flowers\, premiered on Hulu on Ja
	nuary 17\, 2025\, earning widespread critical acclaim. He is also the host
	 of CNN’s Have I Got News for You\, an American adaptation of the long-run
	ning UK comedy series. \nWood Jr. recently released his debut memoir The M
	an of Many Fathers with Crown Publishing (October 2025) and will appear al
	ongside Keanu Reeves and Jonah Hill in the upcoming comedy film Outcome. F
	orbes has called him “One of comedy’s best journalists\,” and Variety name
	d him “One of 10 Comics to Watch.” \nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday\, Augus
	t 27\, 2026 \nShow Time: 8:30 PM HST (Doors open at 8:00 PM) \nVenue: Blue
	 Note Hawaii\, 2335 Kalakaua Avenue\, Honolulu\, HI 96815 \nAge Restrictio
	n: 18+ Event — Valid photo ID required at entry \nContent Warning: Adult l
	anguage and mature themes \nAbout the Venue\nBlue Note Hawaii is Honolulu’
	s most celebrated intimate live entertainment venue\, located at 2335 Kala
	kaua Avenue in the heart of Waikiki. As part of the iconic Blue Note Jazz 
	Club brand\, this venue has hosted some of the world’s greatest performers
	 in an atmosphere that blends tropical island charm with sophisticated nig
	htlife. \nThe venue offers communal seating on a first come\, first served
	 basis — arriving early is strongly recommended to secure the best seats. 
	A full bar and complete dinner menu are available throughout the show\, wi
	th a $20 food or beverage minimum per person. The intimate layout ensures 
	excellent sightlines from virtually every seat in the house. \nBlue Note H
	awaii’s warm\, inviting atmosphere makes it the perfect setting for an eve
	ning of world-class comedy. Parking is available throughout the Waikiki ar
	ea\, with multiple nearby garages and street parking options within easy w
	alking distance. \nWhat to Expect\nThis late-night show features Roy Wood 
	Jr. performing his signature brand of sharp\, socially observant stand-up 
	comedy. Known for his charismatic delivery and thought-provoking material\
	, Wood Jr. blends current events\, personal storytelling\, and razor-sharp
	 wit into a seamless and unforgettable performance. \nAudiences can expect
	 a polished\, high-energy set from one of comedy’s most respected voices. 
	Wood Jr.’s material is both hilarious and insightful — the kind of comedy 
	that makes you laugh and think at the same time. This is a rare opportunit
	y to see a major comedy headliner in an intimate club setting in Hawaii. \
	nSeating is communal and first come\, first served. Arrive early to enjoy 
	dinner and drinks before the show. This is an 18+ event — please bring val
	id photo ID. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $45.90 – $56.67 (includes 
	fees and taxes) \n\nPremium Seating: $45 + fees\nLoge Seating & Bar Area: 
	$35 + fees\n\nTickets are limited to 6 per order. No refunds or exchanges 
	— all sales are final. This event is 18 and over. \nOfficial TicketsResale
	 Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at
	 no extra cost to you.\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.com/event/roy-wood-jr-liv
	e-at-blue-note-hawaii-late/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/roy-wood-jr-live-at-blue-note-hawaii-l
	ate/
